{
  "_about": "Themes reviews.py sorts feedback into. Patterns are Python regular expressions, matched case-insensitively against the review text, grouped by language (add a key such as \"tr\" or \"fr\" for more). kind is complaint (something users hate) or request (something users want that is missing). Labels can be a string or {\"en\": ..., \"de\": ...}. praise_label (optional, for a complaint theme whose label names the complaint) names the same topic where 4-5 star reviews praise it, so the praise list and the battle card say 'Fast, no waiting', not 'Slow, laggy, heavy'; without one they use label. Edit freely and add the category's own words (for a booking app: double booking, time zone, no-show; for a shop: the brand's product names). switch_patterns find reviews that say the writer left, cancelled or is looking for something else. In a pattern, {alt} marks where a named alternative stands: the words there are reported as the alternative only when they start with a capital letter or a digit (copied, never guessed), and a pattern with {alt} only counts when it finds such a name. The shipped patterns are written in the first person (I, we, or a sentence that starts with the verb), so 'the salon cancelled my appointment' or 'let me switch to dark mode' do not count as someone leaving; add the category's own leaving words in the same way. A number alone or a common word that German or a UI capitalises (Konkurrenten, Anbieter, Dark Mode, Premium) is never reported as a name.",
  "switch_patterns": {
      "en": [
          "\\b(i|we)('ve| have| had)?( finally| just| already| now| then| all)? (switched|migrated) (over |back |away )?(to|from)\\b",
          "^(switched|migrated) (over |back |away )?(to|from)\\b",
          "\\b(i|we)('re| are|'m| am)( now| currently)? (switching|migrating) (over |back |away )?(to|from)\\b",
          "\\b(i|we)('ve| have| had)?( finally| just| already| now| then| all)? moved (over to|back to|away from)\\b",
          "\\b(i|we)('ve| have| had)?( finally| just| already| now| then| all)? moved (over |back )?to (a |an |another |the )?(different |new |other )?(app|tool|software|provider|system|solution|competitor|platform|service)\\b",
          "(^|\\b(i|we|and|so|then)('ve| have| had)?( finally| just| already| now| then| also)? )cancel+ed\\b(?! (my |our |the |a |an |this |that |all |every |two |three |several )?(\\w+ )?(appointments?|bookings?|meetings?|events?|orders?|reservations?|sessions?|calls?|classes|lessons?|slots?|visits?)\\b)",
          "\\bcancel+(ed|ing) (my|our) (subscription|account|plan|membership|contract|licen[cs]e)\\b",
          "\\bunsubscribed\\b(?! from (the |their |all |your )?(e-?mails?|newsletters?|mailing|marketing|notifications?|sms|texts?)\\b)",
          "\\blooking for (an |another )?alternatives?\\b",
          "\\b(i|we)('ll| will|'m going to| am going to|'re going to| are going to|'m gonna| am gonna|'m about to| am about to|'re about to| are about to) (cancel|uninstall|leave|switch (to|from|away|providers|tools|apps))\\b(?! (a |an |this |my |our )?(reviews?|comments?|feedback|ratings?|notes?|messages?|tips?)\\b)(?! (my |our |the |a |an |this |that |all |every |two |three |several )?(\\w+ )?(appointments?|bookings?|meetings?|events?|orders?|reservations?|sessions?|calls?|classes|lessons?|slots?|visits?)\\b)",
          "\\buninstall(ed|ing)\\b(?! and (then )?re-?install)",
          "\\bdeleted (the|this) app\\b",
          "\\breplaced (it|them|this) with\\b",
          "(\\b(i|we)('ve| have| had|'re| are|'m| am)?( finally| just| already| now| then| all| currently)? |^|(?<=[.!?]\\s))(switched|switching|migrated|migrating) (over |back )?(from [^.!?,]{1,40}? )?to {alt}",
          "\\bwe('ve| have| had)?( finally| just| already| now| then| all)? moved (over |back )?(from [^.!?,]{1,40}? )?to {alt}",
          "\\bi('ve| have| had)?( finally| just| already| now| then)? moved (over to|back to|from [^.!?,]{1,40}? to) {alt}",
          "(\\b(i|we)('m| am|'re| are|'ll| will)? |^|(?<=[.!?]\\s))(going|went|go) back to {alt}",
          "\\b(i|we)('ve| have| had|'re| are|'m| am)?( finally| just| already| now)? (left|leaving) \\w+ for {alt}",
          "\\breplaced (it|them|this) with {alt}"
      ],
      "de": [
          "\\b(bin|sind)\\b[^.!?]{0,60}\\bgewechselt\\b",
